Infrastructure and deploy tasks (infra/README.md, docs/CI.md). The app's own TODO is ../TODO.

deploys (.github/workflows/deploy.yml)
- deploy on every merge to main: add `push: branches: [main]` to deploy.yml and remove `push` from
  terraform.yml (its plan and apply jobs are in deploy.yml too). Google stacks are the last thing a
  deploy can depend on that is still applied by hand
- a scheduled deploy run: merges made with a workflow's token (Dependabot's auto-merge) start no other
  workflow, so a merge it makes would never be deployed
- the rollback (`wrangler rollback` after a failed smoke test) has never run: try it once on purpose
- the production deploy token (`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` in `production`) has no expiry check yet
  (`scripts/ci/check-expiry.sh` knows the Terraform ones); give it a CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN_EXPIRES variable
  and check it in the deploy job
- the Worker bundle's hash in the deploy's message (`wrangler deploy --message`), so the dashboard's
  versions say which build they are

tokens
- check the bootstrap script the next time it is used: the template URL fills in only the permission
  and the name (its key, `account_api_tokens`, is from memory; the first try showed the form had no
  expiry, IP or account limit), and the script now refuses a token with no end date or one past two
  hours, no IP limit, or other than this account's resources. Those checks read
  GET /accounts/<id>/tokens/<id>: confirm its fields (`condition.request_ip.in`, `policies[].resources`)

Terraform in CI
- the Google stacks (google-chordless, google-dev), by Workload Identity Federation: nothing stored.
  Never give Terraform API Tokens: Edit, which is as much as the account

cloudflare
- HSTS (Strict-Transport-Security): a zone setting in infra/cloudflare; ZAP's rule 10035 then
  becomes FAIL in .zap/rules.tsv

google
- the Team storage service account should move to a Google Cloud project of its own:
  docs/CLOUD_MIGRATION.md, step 6

github
- agents with a GitHub identity of their own, so a pull request can need an approval (infra/github's
  required_approvals)
